<title>FRANCE: Lyonnaise relaxed on 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Lyonnaise relaxed on 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French utilities company Lyonnaise des Eaux has no reason to worry about its 1996 results, deputy chairman Guy de Panafieu said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no reason to change our ideas. There is nothing to cause concern on our results for 1996, on the contrary,&quot; he said at a news conference.</p>
<p>Chairman Jerome Monod said last September that the full-year result could see a rise of around the same amount as that seen in the first half, which was 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
